#: ../../../glossary.rst:-1
msgid "Glossary of terms used throughout the Spack documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:46
msgid "Glossary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:48
msgid ""
"This page collects definitions for the terms that appear throughout the "
"Spack documentation. For an alphabetic list of every documented keyword and "
"environment variable, see the :ref:`general index <genindex>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:59
msgid "abstract spec"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:61
msgid ""
"A :term:`spec` that is only partially specified. Missing fields (version, "
"variants, compiler, dependencies) are filled in during :term:"
"`concretization`. Anything a user types on the command line is an abstract "
"spec until it is concretized. See also :term:`concrete spec`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:314
msgid "anonymous environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:315
msgid "independent environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:317
msgid ""
"An :term:`environment` activated by directory path (``spack env activate ./"
"my-env``). Not registered under a name. See :ref:`independent_environments`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:91
msgid "anonymous spec"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:93
msgid ""
"A spec without a package name, used to express constraints that should apply "
"to any package matching it (for example as selection patterns in "
"configuration files). See :ref:`anonymous_specs`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:128
msgid "architecture spec"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:130
msgid ""
"The platform, operating system, and :term:`target` :term:`microarchitecture` "
"for a build, written as ``arch=platform-os-target`` (e.g. ``arch=linux-"
"ubuntu22.04-zen3``). See :ref:`architecture_specifiers`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:344
msgid "binary mirror"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:345
msgid "buildcache"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:347
msgid ""
"A :term:`mirror` that hosts pre-built binary packages. Spack can both push "
"to and install from build caches. See :doc:`binary_caches`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:358
msgid "bootstrap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:360
msgid ""
"The process by which Spack provisions its own runtime dependencies "
"(``clingo``, ``gnupg``, patchelf) on a fresh system. See :doc:"
"`bootstrapping`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:201
msgid "build cache index"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:203
msgid ""
"A JSON manifest in a :term:`buildcache` listing every binary it contains "
"together with their hashes and dependencies. The :term:`concretizer` "
"downloads it (or its manifest equivalent in an :term:`OCI buildcache`) to "
"decide which binaries are eligible for :term:`reuse` without fetching every "
"individual spec. Refreshed with ``spack buildcache update-index`` and "
"``spack buildcache push --update-index``; see :ref:`binary_caches`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:191
msgid "build environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:193
msgid ""
"The shell environment Spack constructs for a package's build: ``PATH``, "
"``CC`` / ``CXX`` / ``FC`` pointing at the :term:`compiler wrappers <compiler "
"wrapper>`, ``CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH``, ``PKG_CONFIG_PATH``, :term:`jobserver` "
"``MAKEFLAGS``, and any variables set by ``setup_build_environment`` or by "
"dependencies' ``setup_dependent_build_environment``. Variables that could "
"pull unintended system libraries into the build (``LD_LIBRARY_PATH``, "
"``CPATH``, ``LIBRARY_PATH``, ``PYTHONPATH``, ...) are unset. ``spack build-"
"env <spec>`` prints it; passing a shell as the command (``spack build-env "
"<spec> sh``) drops you into it, and ``--dump`` / ``--pickle`` write it to a "
"file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:370
msgid "build job"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:372
msgid ""
"A unit of work scheduled against the :term:`jobserver` (e.g. a single ``cc`` "
"invocation). ``spack install -j<N>`` (or ``config:build_jobs``) caps the "
"total number of in-flight build jobs across all concurrently building "
"packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:155
msgid "build system"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:157
msgid ""
"A :term:`mixin` base class that knows how to drive a particular build tool: "
"``Package``, :class:`~spack_repo.builtin.build_systems.cmake.CMakePackage`, :"
"class:`~spack_repo.builtin.build_systems.autotools.AutotoolsPackage`, :class:"
"`~spack_repo.builtin.build_systems.meson.MesonPackage`, and so on. See :doc:"
"`build_systems`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:446
msgid "chained install tree"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:448
msgid ""
"A read-only :term:`upstream` :term:`store` made available to a downstream "
"Spack instance so its installs can be reused. See :doc:`chain`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:437
msgid "CI pipeline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:439
msgid ""
"A generated GitLab pipeline that builds and pushes binaries for the specs in "
"an :term:`environment`. See :doc:`pipelines`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:257
msgid "clingo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:259
msgid ""
"The Answer Set Programming (ASP) solver used by the :term:`concretizer`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:135
msgid "compiler flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:137
msgid ""
"Flags injected at build time via :term:`spec syntax`, namespaced by "
"language: ``cflags``, ``cxxflags``, ``fflags``, ``cppflags``, ``ldflags``, "
"``ldlibs``. See :ref:`compiler_flags`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:139
msgid "compiler wrapper"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:141
msgid ""
"A shell script that sits between the build system and the real compiler: it "
"rewrites the command line, injects include, library, and :term:`RPATH` flags "
"for dependencies, and then invokes the underlying compiler. The wrappers are "
"provided by the ``compiler-wrapper`` package, which is automatically "
"injected as a dependency of every package that depends on a language virtual "
"(``c``, ``cxx``, ``fortran``); the :term:`build environment` points ``CC`` / "
"``CXX`` / ``FC`` at the wrapper executables. See :ref:`compiler-wrappers`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:65
msgid "concrete spec"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:67
msgid ""
"A fully specified :term:`spec` in which every field is fixed: an exact "
"version, all variant values, a compiler, an architecture, and a concrete "
"spec for every dependency in the :term:`DAG`. Concrete specs are what Spack "
"actually installs; they are identified by a :term:`DAG hash`. See also :term:"
"`abstract spec`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:248
msgid "concretization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:250
msgid ""
"The process of turning an :term:`abstract spec` and the surrounding "
"configuration into a :term:`concrete spec` DAG. Performed by the :term:"
"`concretizer`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:252
msgid "concretizer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:254
msgid ""
"Spack's solver. The current implementation translates specs and package "
"constraints to Answer Set Programming, runs ``clingo``, and reads concrete "
"specs back out. See :ref:`concretizer-options`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:374
msgid "concurrent packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:376
msgid ""
"The maximum number of packages Spack builds in parallel, controlled by "
"``spack install -p<N>`` / ``--concurrent-packages``. Unbounded by default; "
"packages start as :term:`jobserver` tokens become available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:413
msgid "config.yaml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:415
msgid ""
"The top-level configuration file controlling install paths, build "
"concurrency, locks, modules, and similar settings. See :doc:`config_yaml`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:441
msgid "container image"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:443
msgid ""
"A Docker/OCI image of a Spack-built software stack. Spack can produce one "
"either by exporting already-installed specs with ``spack buildcache push --"
"base-image`` to an OCI registry, or by generating a ``Dockerfile`` / "
"Singularity definition from an :term:`environment` with ``spack "
"containerize``. See :doc:`containers`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:243
msgid "DAG"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:245
msgid ""
"Directed acyclic graph. A concretized spec is a DAG whose nodes are concrete "
"specs and whose edges are dependencies. It is generally not a tree, because "
"dependencies are shared, and the same package may even appear more than once "
"in different configurations or roles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:297
msgid "DAG hash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:299
msgid ""
"The cryptographic hash that identifies a :term:`concrete spec`. Computed "
"over the full DAG (name, version, variants, compiler, flags, arch, and "
"dependency hashes). Used as the directory suffix in the :term:`prefix` and "
"as the spec's primary key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:289
msgid "database"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:291
msgid ""
"The JSON-backed index of every installed spec in the :term:`store`. Acts as "
"a cache so Spack does not need to walk the install tree."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:167
msgid "dependency type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:169
msgid ""
"The role a dependency plays: ``build`` (only needed during the build), "
"``link`` (linked into the dependent), ``run`` (needed at run time), or "
"``test`` (needed only when running tests). A single ``depends_on`` may carry "
"multiple types. See :ref:`dependency-types`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:468
msgid "deprecate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:469
msgid "deprecation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:471
msgid ""
"Marking a version (or whole package) as no longer supported. Package authors "
"set ``deprecated=True`` on a ``version(...)`` :term:`directive`; ``spack "
"install`` then warns and prompts before fetching such a version (``spack "
"install --deprecated`` or ``config:deprecated:true`` skips the check), and "
"``spack info`` lists it under \"Deprecated versions\". Distinct from ``spack "
"deprecate``, which replaces one installed spec with another in the :term:"
"`store` by symlinking the old :term:`prefix` at the new one. See :ref:"
"`deprecate`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:334
msgid "develop spec"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:336
msgid ""
"A spec that builds from a local source directory instead of a fetched "
"archive, so edits to the sources trigger a rebuild on the next install. It "
"carries a ``dev_path=<path>`` variant pointing at the working tree, and is "
"set up with ``spack develop``. See :ref:`cmd-spack-develop`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:172
msgid "direct dependency"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:174
msgid ""
"A dependency that appears in a package's own ``depends_on`` declarations, i."
"e. one edge away in the :term:`DAG`. In :doc:`spec_syntax` the ``%`` :term:"
"`sigil` constrains direct dependencies (``hdf5 %gcc@15``); contrast with :"
"term:`transitive dependency`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:152
msgid "directive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:154
msgid ""
"A function called directly in the class body of a ``package.py`` to declare "
"package metadata: ``version``, ``depends_on``, ``variant``, ``provides``, "
"``conflicts``, ``requires``, ``patch``, ``resource``, ``extends``, and so on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:306
msgid "environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:308
msgid ""
"A named, declarative collection of root specs plus configuration, stored in "
"``spack.yaml``, concretized to ``spack.lock``. The unit of reproducible "
"deployments in Spack. See :doc:`environments`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:75
msgid "explicit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:77
msgid ""
"A property of an installed spec recorded in the :term:`database`. A spec is "
"*explicit* if it was requested directly: a ``spack install`` argument or an :"
"term:`environment` :term:`root spec <root>`. Explicit installs are preserved "
"by ``spack gc``. ``spack mark -e/-i`` toggles the flag on an existing "
"install, ``spack find --explicit`` / ``--implicit`` filters by it, and a :"
"term:`spec group` with ``explicit: false`` installs its specs as implicit. "
"See also :term:`implicit`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:223
msgid "extension"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:225
msgid ""
"A package installed into another package's prefix-like namespace, most "
"commonly a Python extension installed into a Python ``site-packages`` :term:"
"`view`. See :ref:`packaging_extensions`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:227
msgid "external package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:229
msgid ""
"A package that is *not* built by Spack but found on the system and "
"registered through :term:`packages.yaml`. Used for vendor-provided "
"compilers, MPI, CUDA, system libraries, etc. See :ref:`sec-external-"
"packages`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:378
msgid "fetch strategy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:380
msgid ""
"The mechanism used to obtain a package's source: a URL tarball, or a "
"checkout from ``git``, ``hg``, ``svn``, or ``cvs``. See :ref:`vcs-fetch`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:86
msgid "fresh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:88
msgid ""
"The :term:`concretizer` policy of ignoring already-installed and cached "
"specs and solving for the newest configuration allowed by the constraints. "
"Selected with ``spack install --fresh`` / ``spack concretize --fresh``; the "
"opposite of :term:`reuse`. ``--fresh-roots`` is a middle ground: solve :term:"
"`root specs <root>` fresh while still reusing their dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:390
msgid "hook"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:392
msgid ""
"A Python callback built into Spack that runs at a defined point in the "
"install lifecycle (post-install, pre-uninstall, ...), for example to "
"generate :term:`module files <module file>` or rewrite shebang lines (:term:"
"`sbang`). Hooks are fixed in Spack itself; packages instead customize their "
"own builds by wrapping :term:`phases <phase>` with ``@run_before`` / "
"``@run_after``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:82
msgid "implicit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:84
msgid ""
"The opposite of :term:`explicit`: a property of an installed spec, recorded "
"in the :term:`database`, marking that it was only installed as a dependency "
"of something else. Implicit installs become eligible for garbage collection "
"(``spack gc``) once no installed spec depends on them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:433
msgid "include chain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:435
msgid ""
"A sequence of ``include:`` directives pulling additional YAML files (or :"
"term:`environments <environment>`) into a configuration. See :doc:"
"`include_yaml`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:282
msgid "install tree"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:284
msgid "See :term:`store`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:365
msgid "jobserver"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:367
msgid ""
"A POSIX jobserver, compatible with GNU Make's protocol, that bounds the "
"total number of concurrent :term:`build jobs <build job>` across all "
"packages building in parallel. Spack creates one when ``-j<N>`` is passed "
"(or inherits an external one from ``MAKEFLAGS``) and forwards it to every "
"package's :term:`build environment`. See :ref:`installing`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:398
msgid "Lmod"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:400
msgid ""
"A Lua-based module system Spack can generate :term:`module files <module "
"file>` for. See also :term:`TCL modules`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:311
msgid "managed environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:313
msgid ""
"An :term:`environment` stored in Spack's environment directory and addressed "
"by name (``spack env activate myenv``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:293
msgid "manifest"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:295
msgid ""
"The ``spack.yaml`` file describing an :term:`environment`: the root specs, "
"configuration overrides, and :term:`view` settings. Concretizing the "
"manifest produces the :term:`spack.lock` lockfile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:459
msgid "microarchitecture"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:461
msgid ""
"A specific CPU microarchitecture recognized by ``archspec`` (``zen3``, "
"``skylake_avx512``, ``neoverse_v2``, ...) and used as the :term:`target` "
"portion of an :term:`architecture spec`. The :term:`concretizer` can label "
"nodes either with full microarchitectures or with generic families "
"(``x86_64_v3``) via ``concretizer:targets:granularity``. See :ref:"
"`concretizer-options`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:339
msgid "mirror"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:341
msgid ""
"A location (URL or path) holding copies of the artifacts Spack would "
"otherwise fetch from their canonical locations: source tarballs, :term:"
"`resources <resource>`, and :term:`patches <patch>` for source builds, and "
"binary tarballs in the case of a :term:`binary mirror`. Mirrors are "
"consulted before fetching upstream. See :doc:`mirrors`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:421
msgid "mirrors.yaml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:423
msgid ""
"Configuration of source and binary :term:`mirrors <mirror>`. See :doc:"
"`mirrors`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:480
msgid "mixin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:482
msgid ""
"A package base class that contributes variants, dependencies, and helper "
"methods without being a full :term:`build system` on its own. :class:"
"`~spack_repo.builtin.build_systems.cuda.CudaPackage`, :class:`~spack_repo."
"builtin.build_systems.rocm.ROCmPackage`, and :class:`~spack_repo.builtin."
"build_systems.sourceforge.SourceforgePackage` are typical examples, combined "
"with a concrete build system via multiple inheritance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:394
msgid "module file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:396
msgid ""
"A generated file (Lua for :term:`Lmod`, TCL for environment-modules) that "
"loads a package's run environment into the user's shell. See :doc:"
"`module_file_support` and :ref:`modules-yaml`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:196
msgid "module set"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:198
msgid ""
"A named block under ``modules:`` in ``modules.yaml`` that produces its own "
"collection of :term:`module files <module file>` with its own install root, "
"naming scheme, and inclusion rules. The default set is called ``default``; "
"module commands target it unless ``--name <set>`` is given. See :ref:"
"`modules-yaml`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:425
msgid "modules.yaml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:427
msgid ""
"Configuration of :term:`module file` generation. See :doc:"
"`module_file_support`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:238
msgid "namespace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:240
msgid ""
"A repo's identifier (``repo.yaml``'s ``namespace:`` key). Fully qualified "
"package names take the form ``namespace.name`` (e.g. ``builtin.zlib``). See :"
"ref:`namespaces`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:484
msgid "non-redistributable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:486
msgid ""
"A package whose source or binaries may not be republished, expressed with "
"the ``redistribute(source=False, binary=False, when=...)`` :term:"
"`directive`. ``spack mirror create`` and ``spack buildcache push`` skip such "
"artifacts by default; ``--private`` opts them back in for internal :term:"
"`mirrors <mirror>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:350
msgid "OCI buildcache"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:352
msgid ""
"A :term:`buildcache` layered into an OCI registry (Docker Hub, GHCR, ...) so "
"binaries can be distributed alongside :term:`container images <container "
"image>`. See :ref:`binary_caches_oci`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:144
msgid "package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:146
msgid ""
"A Python class describing how to fetch, configure, build, and install a "
"piece of software; also called a *recipe*. Lives in a ``package.py`` file "
"inside a :term:`repository <repo>`. See :doc:`package_fundamentals`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:302
msgid "package hash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:304
msgid ""
"A hash of the ``package.py`` source (and its build inputs), tracked so Spack "
"can detect :term:`recipe` changes. Distinct from the :term:`DAG hash`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:417
msgid "packages.yaml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:419
msgid ""
"Per-package configuration: :term:`external packages <external package>`, "
"version preferences, :term:`requirements <requirement>`, variants. See :doc:"
"`packages_yaml`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:215
msgid "patch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:217
msgid ""
"A source patch applied to a package before configuring. Declared with the "
"``patch(...)`` :term:`directive`; see :ref:`patching`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:181
msgid "phase"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:182
msgid "build phase"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:183
msgid "install phase"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:185
msgid ""
"One step of a :term:`build system`'s install lifecycle. The ordered list "
"lives in the builder's ``phases`` attribute, for example ``(\"configure\", "
"\"build\", \"install\")`` for autotools or ``(\"cmake\", \"build\", "
"\"install\")`` for CMake. Each phase is a method on the builder class and "
"can be overridden, replaced, or wrapped with ``@run_before`` / "
"``@run_after``. The final ``install`` phase is the one that copies the build "
"results into the installation :term:`prefix`. Note that *build phase* is "
"often used loosely for any phase in the lifecycle, not just for the phase "
"named ``build``. See :ref:`overriding-phases`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:285
msgid "prefix"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:287
msgid ""
"The installation directory of a single concrete spec inside the :term:"
"`store`. The default layout is ``<platform>-<target>/<name>-<version>-"
"<hash>`` relative to the store root."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:104
msgid "propagation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:106
msgid ""
"Pushing a variant value, compiler flag, or dependency choice down through a "
"spec's dependencies. Written with doubled :term:`sigils <sigil>`: ``+"
"+variant`` and ``cflags==-O3`` propagate a variant or flag, while ``%%c,"
"cxx=clang`` propagates a :term:`direct dependency` choice (typically the "
"compiler) to the runtime sub-DAG as a :term:`strong preference`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:464
msgid "provenance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:466
msgid ""
"Recorded information about how an install was produced: the source checksum "
"or git commit, the compiler and its flags, the :term:`patches <patch>` "
"applied, and any develop-source path. Spack tracks provenance in the per-"
"install ``install_manifest.json``, in the :term:`SBOM`, and in spec metadata "
"such as the ``commit`` variant for git-based versions and the ``dev_path`` "
"variant for :term:`develop specs <develop spec>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:163
msgid "provider"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:165
msgid ""
"A package that satisfies a :term:`virtual package`. For example, ``openmpi`` "
"and ``mpich`` both provide ``mpi``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:149
msgid "recipe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:151
msgid "See :term:`package`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:232
msgid "repo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:233
msgid "repository"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:235
msgid ""
"A directory tree containing package :term:`recipes <recipe>` plus a ``repo."
"yaml``. Multiple repos can be layered, each contributing packages under a :"
"term:`namespace`. See :doc:`repositories`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:429
msgid "repos.yaml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:431
msgid ""
"The list of active package :term:`repositories <repo>`. See :doc:"
"`repositories`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:264
msgid "requirement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:266
msgid ""
"A hard constraint declared in ``packages.yaml`` under ``require:``. The :"
"term:`concretizer` must satisfy it or fail. See :ref:`package-requirements`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:219
msgid "resource"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:221
msgid ""
"An extra archive fetched alongside the main source and unpacked under the "
"build :term:`stage`. Declared with the ``resource(...)`` :term:`directive`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:260
msgid "reuse"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:262
msgid ""
"The :term:`concretizer` policy of preferring already-installed or cached "
"specs over rebuilding from scratch. Tunable through ``concretizer:reuse``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:70
msgid "root spec"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:71
msgid "root"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:73
msgid ""
"A spec the user requested directly: an argument to ``spack install`` or an "
"entry in an :term:`environment`'s ``spack.yaml`` ``specs:`` list. Roots are "
"the starting points of concretization; everything else in the resulting :"
"term:`DAG` is a dependency pulled in to satisfy a root."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:385
msgid "RPATH"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:386
msgid "runpath"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:388
msgid ""
"A linker-embedded library search path baked into installed binaries so they "
"find their dependencies without ``LD_LIBRARY_PATH``. See :ref:"
"`handling_rpaths` and :ref:`shared-linking-type`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:488
msgid "sandbox"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:489
msgid "sandboxing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:491
msgid ""
"An opt-in Linux build isolation mode that confines a package's :term:`build "
"phase` using Landlock, restricting filesystem and (optionally) network "
"access. Configured under ``config:sandbox:`` with ``allow_read`` / "
"``allow_write`` paths and an ``allow_network`` toggle; intended for "
"reproducibility and bug containment, not as a strict security boundary. See :"
"doc:`installing`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:382
msgid "sbang"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:384
msgid ""
"Tool that lets Spack use shebang (``#!``) lines whose length exceeds the "
"operating system's limit, by rewriting them through a post-install :term:"
"`hook`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:475
msgid "SBOM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:477
msgid ""
"A Software Bill of Materials emitted by Spack in SPDX-2.3 format for every "
"installation. Written under ``<prefix>/.spack/sbom/`` and meets NTIA minimum "
"elements. See :ref:`sbom`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:406
msgid "scope"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:407
msgid "configuration scope"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:409
msgid ""
"A named layer of YAML configuration. Examples are the ``defaults`` scope "
"shipped with Spack, the ``site`` scope for a single Spack instance, and the "
"``user`` scope in ``~/.spack``; settings in higher-precedence scopes "
"override lower ones, and command-line flags override them all. ``spack "
"config scopes`` lists the active scopes in precedence order. See :ref:"
"`configuration-scopes`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:99
msgid "sigil"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:100
msgid "spec sigil"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:102
msgid ""
"A punctuation token that introduces the next component of a spec in :term:"
"`spec syntax`: ``@`` (version), ``%`` (:term:`direct dependency`, including "
"compilers), ``^`` (:term:`transitive dependency`), ``+`` / ``~`` (boolean :"
"term:`variants <variant>`), ``/`` (:term:`DAG hash`), and the doubled forms "
"``++`` / ``~~`` / ``==`` / ``%%`` for :term:`propagation`. Each sigil is "
"also indexed individually under *spec sigil* in the :ref:`general index "
"<genindex>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:354
msgid "signing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:356
msgid ""
"Cryptographic signing of :term:`buildcache` contents with GPG so installers "
"can verify :term:`provenance`. See :doc:`signing`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:206
msgid "spack instance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:208
msgid ""
"A Spack installation itself, addressable in config as ``$spack``. In the "
"context of :term:`chained install trees <chained install tree>`, \":term:"
"`upstream` instance\" is often used informally to refer to that instance's :"
"term:`store`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:323
msgid "spack.lock"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:325
msgid ""
"The concretized lockfile of an :term:`environment`: a frozen DAG of concrete "
"specs that Spack reuses across activations and machines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:320
msgid "spack.yaml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:322
msgid ""
"The human-edited manifest of an :term:`environment`: the specs to build, the "
"configuration overrides, and the :term:`view` settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:53
msgid "spec"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:55
msgid ""
"A description of a package configuration: name, version, variants, compiler, "
"flags, architecture, and dependencies. Specs are Spack's central data "
"structure and the syntax users type on the command line. See :doc:"
"`spec_syntax` and :ref:`sec-specs`. See also :term:`abstract spec`, :term:"
"`concrete spec`, :term:`root spec <root>`, :term:`anonymous spec`, :term:"
"`spec syntax`, :term:`explicit`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:330
msgid "spec group"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:332
msgid ""
"A named set of specs inside an :term:`environment`, sharing constraints and "
"concretization rules. See :ref:`environment-spec-groups`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:95
msgid "spec syntax"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:97
msgid ""
"The textual language used to write specs, built from :term:`sigils <spec "
"sigil>`: version (``@``), :term:`direct dependencies <direct dependency>` "
"including compilers (``%``), :term:`transitive dependencies <transitive "
"dependency>` (``^``), variants (``+`` / ``~`` / ``name=value``), flags "
"(``cflags=...``), architecture (``arch=...``), and hashes (``/``). See :doc:"
"`spec_syntax`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:454
msgid "splicing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:456
msgid ""
"Replacing a dependency in a :term:`concrete spec` with a different, ABI-"
"compatible spec providing the same package or :term:`virtual package`. Often "
"used to swap a generic :term:`buildcache` MPI for a site-tuned one. See :ref:"
"`splicing` and :ref:`abi_compatibility`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:362
msgid "stage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:364
msgid ""
"The temporary working directory where a package's sources are unpacked and "
"built."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:210
msgid "stand-alone test"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:212
msgid ""
"A test defined by a package's ``test_*`` methods and executed *after* "
"installation by ``spack test run`` against an installed :term:`prefix`. "
"Distinct from build-time tests run during the ``check`` :term:`build phase` "
"of an autotools/cmake build. See :ref:`cmd-spack-test` and the testing "
"section of the packaging guide."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:113
msgid "sticky variant"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:115
msgid ""
"A variant the :term:`concretizer` is not allowed to flip silently. The user "
"(or a :term:`requirement`) must set its value explicitly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:278
msgid "store"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:280
msgid ""
"The directory tree where Spack installs packages, one :term:`prefix` per "
"concrete spec; also called the *install tree*. Backed by a :term:`database` "
"that indexes every install."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:269
msgid "strong preference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:271
msgid ""
"A soft constraint declared in ``packages.yaml`` under ``prefer:``. The :term:"
"`concretizer` tries to satisfy it, but may ignore it if it cannot be met. "
"See :ref:`package-strong-preferences`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:132
msgid "target"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:134
msgid ""
"The :term:`microarchitecture` portion of an :term:`architecture spec`, "
"resolved by ``archspec`` (e.g. ``zen3``, ``skylake_avx512``, "
"``neoverse_v2``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:402
msgid "TCL modules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:404
msgid ""
"The module system of the ``environment-modules`` project, whose module files "
"are written in TCL. One of the two module systems Spack generates :term:"
"`module files <module file>` for; the other is :term:`Lmod`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:274
msgid "toolchain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:276
msgid ""
"A reusable bundle of compiler and library choices that packages can opt "
"into, configured in ``toolchains.yaml``. See :doc:`toolchains_yaml`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:176
msgid "transitive dependency"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:178
msgid ""
"A dependency reachable through one or more intermediate packages, i.e. a "
"dependency of a dependency. The ``^`` :term:`sigil` constrains transitive "
"dependencies (``hdf5 ^hwloc+cuda``). A :term:`view`'s ``link: run`` / "
"``link: all`` options pull in :term:`root spec <root>` transitive "
"dependencies of the corresponding :term:`types <dependency type>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:450
msgid "upstream"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:452
msgid ""
"Another :term:`spack instance` whose :term:`store` is registered (via "
"``upstreams.yaml``) as a read-only source of installed packages for the "
"local instance. See :doc:`chain`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:108
msgid "variant"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:110
msgid ""
"A named build option on a package. Variants can be boolean (``+mpi`` / "
"``~mpi``), single-valued (``build_type=Release``), or multi-valued "
"(``fabrics=verbs,psm``). See :ref:`basic-variants`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:117
msgid "version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:119
msgid ""
"A specific release of a package, declared in ``package.py`` with the "
"``version(...)`` :term:`directive`. Versions are ordered and can be "
"compared, e.g. ``@1.2:1.4``. See :ref:`version-specifier`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:125
msgid "version list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:127
msgid "A comma-separated set of versions or ranges, e.g. ``@1.2,1.4:1.6``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:122
msgid "version range"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:124
msgid ""
"A constraint of the form ``@low:high``, ``@low:``, or ``@:high`` that "
"matches any version inside the interval."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:326
msgid "view"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:328
msgid ""
"A unified directory (symlinks, hardlinks, or copies) projecting an :term:"
"`environment`'s installs into one tree, suitable for ``PATH``-style use. "
"See :ref:`configuring_environment_views`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:159
msgid "virtual package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../glossary.rst:161
msgid ""
"A name (such as ``mpi``, ``blas``, ``lapack``, or ``c``) that represents an "
"interface rather than a concrete implementation. Real packages :term:"
"`provide <provider>` virtuals."
msgstr ""
